{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And in all that I have said to you.</b> From everything I warned you about regarding the Sabbaths of other years, you must keep [the Sabbaths] of the Sabbatical year. Another interpretation: not regarding the rest of an ox, donkey, and maidservant alone do I warn you, but regarding everything that requires cessation I warn you, such as utensils. Another interpretation: <b>and in all that I have said to you</b> — from the day the Ten Commandments were given until now. <b>You shall keep</b> — you shall be careful; it turns back and includes all his warnings, as in 'cursed be he who does not uphold,' etc. Another interpretation: a warning for all positive commandments, as Rashi explained. From here they said throughout the Talmud: a positive commandment pushes aside a negative commandment, for within a positive commandment there is a negative commandment with it, since 'you shall keep' constitutes a negative commandment. Another interpretation: <b>and in all that I have said to you, you shall keep.</b> It does not refer to a positive commandment, for if it referred to a positive commandment, then every positive commandment would be included in a negative commandment — as we say: wherever 'take heed lest' or 'do not' is stated, it is nothing but a negative commandment, and where would one find a positive commandment alone without a negative?" "<b>And the name of other elohim.</b> It is juxtaposed here to say: in all that I have said to you, you may mention — but not the name of other elohim."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The fifth interpretation's opening phrase reads 'לא קאי הוא אלא אלא תעשה' with apparent doubling of אלא; translated as 'It does not refer to [לאו], but rather to a positive commandment [עשה],' reading the first אלא as לאו based on context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:05.740304840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}